    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0566" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/5–854: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Thailand</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Donovan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-05-08T11:00:00+07:00">May 8, 1954—11
                            a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2237. Re USUN telegram sent Department 678 repeated Bangkok 2. I convinced Prince
                        Narathip,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d310-f1"/> Thai Foreign Minister, should be
                    elected president General Assembly this fall to enable both US and entire free
                    world to benefit from his election as one three chairmen at Korean phase Geneva
                    conference and his strong and valuable speeches made said conference in
                    connection unification Korea. His stand at Geneva <pb facs="0567" n="539"
                        xml:id="pg539"/> on question “Asia for Asians” further demonstrates
                    advantages to be gained his presidency GA. Certain this preferable in Thailand
                    to Thailand selection Security Council. Further convinced Narathip should be
                    informed promptly decision US both vote for and generally support Narathip for
                    presidency GA.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Donovan</hi>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d310-f1" n="1" xml:id="d310-f1-content">
                <p>Also known as Prince Wan.</p>
            </note>
